  "notes": "UK girl group with bootleg/synth-pop DNA: 82–127 straight, backbeat on 2&4, and the research says the mid-tempos have \"a 16th-hat 'walking' feel rather than a club pulse\", which is why the hat is pinned to 16ths at a high fill density while the kick stays off the floor. Three drum facts are authored — \"hard gated snare on 2&4\" (a high accent tier), \"kick on 1 and 3&\" (anchor 1, second anchor \"3&\"), and \"occasional 808-style cowbell/tom\" plus stacked handclaps, which is the cowbell/tom/snap perc block. Three minor tonics are named (F-sharp minor, B minor, D-flat minor) so `keys` is authored. The defining claim is harmonic: \"the electro singles sit on a two-chord ostinato with a bassline doing the harmonic work\", and \"analogue-style square/saw bass playing a riff, not a root — the riff *is* the hook\", so `followRootsProb` falls to 0.35, the bass runs `independent_riff` with authored cell shapes, and the chord block leans on `vamp` with `maxChords` at 3. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities, `bpm.mode` 104 and the bass cell shapes — the research says \"riff\", not which degrees.",
